\* private/fed/client/scheduler_cmds.py:122-136; private/fed/client/client_executor.py:262-305
JobExecutorPrepareException(s) ==
    LET t == T0 IN
    /\ "launchError" \in Faults
    /\ client[s][t].pc \in {"allocated","consumed","checked"}
    /\ jobCP_f' = [jobCP_f EXCEPT !.client = [client EXCEPT ![s][t].pc = "rollback"]]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<net, pJobCP>>

\* private/fed/client/scheduler_cmds.py:122-124 for job B (profile otherJob):
\* B's START handler consumes B's allocation into the process-global env.
\* The server starts one job at a time and waits for its START replies
\* (job_runner.py:355-361; the reply is the handler's return value), so B's
\* handler runs before our START arrives or after we replied (or once the
\* server's wait timed out); e.g. while our CJ restarts.
OtherJobConsume(s) ==
    LET t == T0 IN
    /\ "otherJob" \in Profile
    \* other jobs keep starting on the CP: B (or a later job with B's GPU)
    \* writes again whenever the env is not already B's (v5: was once only, and
    \* random simulation spent it before our START)
    /\ resourceEnv[s] # <<OtherUnit>>
    /\ \/ ~\E k \in jobCP_f.handled[s] : k[1] = "START_JOB"
       \/ jobCP_f.startReply[s] # "none"
       \/ "rpcTimeout" \in Faults
    /\ jobCP_f' = [jobCP_f EXCEPT !.resourceEnv = [resourceEnv EXCEPT ![s] = <<OtherUnit>>],
              !.otherJob[s] = TRUE]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<net, pJobCP>>

